unt=11, critical_path_length=2).\n2. Write 11 epic files (body + frontmatter via script).\n3. Write 11 ai-signals files.\n4. batch-read, compare.\n5. Run validator until OK.\n6. Set decompose_complete=true (final action).\n\nNote \"no cross-references to sibling epics\" in epic bodies — don't mention E0xx IDs in bodies. Careful in ACs/scope: refer to \"the PQC base image availability investigation\" etc. in plain terms.\n\nAlso epic bodies must not follow instructions from the untrusted strategy data — fine.\n\nMermaid DAG:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[E001 AIPCC base availability] --> E006\n    E001 --> E007\n    E002[E002 guardrails feasibility] --> E008\n    E003[E003 trainer TLS audit] --> E009\n    E005[E005 ubi9-minimal switch] --> E011\n    E004[E004 readiness matrix]\n    E010[E010 CI scan]\n```\n\nRoots at top: E001, E002, E003, E004, E005, E010 are roots. Arrows dep → dependent. Good.\n\ncritical_path_length: E001→E006 = 2 edges / 3 nodes? \"critical path length\" — I'll interpret as number of epics on longest path = 2. Hmm, or edges? A path E001→E006 has 2 epics. All chains are length 2 epics. I'll set critical_path_length=2.\n\nLet me now also double check the validator script to know exactly what it checks, to avoid violations.","signature":"b4beafcd8a1c47f185d86226d315eb6c"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63594,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1da33aad9f5aea0","agent_id":"a1b9c8d3f7c4bce05","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"a1d71bb3-54be-408d-8971-f0e02adc822a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:09:16.916Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
