{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9f73c267-0365-43f2-9146-988186d0bbf2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0a1a8f71267a9bf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-n6lpo8ou/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E001.md","content":"# Confirm AIPCC PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase commitment\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's unconfirmed base image dependencies: whether PQC-enabled variants of the `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` base images will exist in time for RHOAI 3.6, and the committed date of the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase that gates adoption of `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` for the RHEL9-ELS-based image family. It tracks the AIPCC spike RHOAIENG-7195 and the rebase AIPCC-7258. The outcome determines, per image family, whether the base image switch campaigns proceed or the affected component teams file OCP exceptions by the September 15, 2026 deadline.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Engage the AIPCC team to enumerate, for each of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22`: whether a PQC variant exists today, is committed with a delivery date, or is not planned.\n- For any candidate variant image that already exists, verify it activates the `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy (the same acceptance bar the strategy sets for the confirmed base images).\n- Obtain the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) and assess its impact on adopting `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` for the ~34 RHEL9-ELS-based RHOAI images (notebooks, workbenches, training runtimes, mlserver).\n- Produce a per-family go/no-go recommendation: switch to a PQC variant/rebased base, or fall back to component-team OCP exceptions filed via OCPEXCEPT.\n- Escalate if no committed date exists by early September, per the strategy's risk mitigation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- For each of the four python/nodejs base images, a documented availability status exists: available now (with verified `DEFAULT:PQ` policy where an image can be inspected), committed with a delivery date, or not planned.\n- The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date is documented, with an explicit impact statement on RHEL9-ELS PQC base adoption for the affected image family.\n- A per-family recommendation (switch vs. OCP exception fallback) is recorded and handed to the compliance tracking effort so every affected image has a decided path.\n- An escalation is raised if any gating dependency has no committed date by early September 2026.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): determines the target PQC base image for the python-based and nodejs-based runtime images and the adoptability of the RHEL9-ELS PQC base.\n- HLR-2 (P0): the per-family switch-vs-exception outcome is the decision input for teams that must file OCP exceptions by September 15.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":76667,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1da33aad9f5aea0","agent_id":"a1b9c8d3f7c4bce05","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"d76a7f08-be5a-4c71-abec-06d0003c96f1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:10:37.085Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
