{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ce8fdfaf-116e-49ab-9458-3f175e22c9f3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a12942b552adaa3e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-n6lpo8ou/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E003.md","content":"# Audit trainer data cache Rust TLS posture\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's unknown TLS posture of the trainer data cache: whether it uses system OpenSSL (via native-tls or an equivalent OpenSSL-backed path), in which case the PQC base image switch alone confers `DEFAULT:PQ` and ML-KEM support, or a pure-Rust TLS stack (rustls with the ring provider), in which case it cannot inherit PQC from a base image and needs a TLS migration or an OCP exception. It tracks audit spike RHOAIENG-7196.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inspect the trainer data cache source and dependency lockfiles to identify its TLS library and crypto provider for both inbound and outbound connections.\n- Determine, from the identified stack, whether the PQC base image switch is sufficient for ML-KEM hybrid key exchange support or whether a provider migration is required.\n- If a pure-Rust stack is found: assess the migration path (ML-KEM-capable provider), estimate effort against the September 15, 2026 deadline, and recommend migrate vs. OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with the migration as remediation.\n- Record the finding in the compliance tracking structure so the trainer data cache image is classified correctly (switch-covered vs. exception/migration path).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The trainer data cache's TLS library and crypto provider are documented, with source references (dependency manifests/lockfiles).\n- A recorded determination: PQC base image switch sufficient (OpenSSL-backed), or ML-KEM-capable TLS migration required (pure-Rust stack).\n- If migration is required: an effort estimate against the September 15, 2026 deadline and a recommendation (migrate vs. OCP exception with remediation plan).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): determines whether the trainer data cache image is covered by the PQC base image switch or needs separate remediation.\n- HLR-2 (P0): the posture outcome is the decision input for the trainer team's exception filing (or avoidance of one) by September 15.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78283,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1da33aad9f5aea0","agent_id":"a1b9c8d3f7c4bce05","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"2b51c3cc-4543-47d3-9c3f-f825e23fb2bc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:11:00.777Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
