{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1a39ea9d-d088-4abc-a7a5-437dea952607","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc2c6d61ffd69e0a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-n6lpo8ou/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E004.md","content":"# PQC Readiness Matrix and aggregated compliance tracking\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic creates and drives the strategy's central coordination deliverables: the PQC Readiness Matrix — a per-image classification of every RHOAI runtime image (current base, target PQC base or exception, TLS stack, owning team, status) — and the aggregated compliance view that gives OCP 5.0 visibility into the September 15, 2026 deadline. It ensures every image is accounted for as switched, in progress via a linked team tracking ticket, or covered by a filed OCP exception, and it drives the exception process for teams that cannot comply.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the PQC Readiness Matrix per component from the RHOAI-Build-Config rhoai-3.5 CSV (153 relatedImages) and the organized image inventory, recording for each image: current base image, target PQC base (`ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or a python/nodejs PQC variant), TLS stack classification (system OpenSSL vs. pure-Rust vs. Java/NSS), owning team, and switch-vs-exception decision.\n- Stand up the aggregated compliance tracking view: all component team tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy, with per-image status roll-up.\n- Drive the exception process: identify teams that cannot comply by September 15, remind teams weekly, and escalate to leadership for any image with neither a switch plan nor a filed exception (per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n- Track the known exception candidates called out by the strategy: fms-guardrails-orchestrator (rustls+ring), the TrustyAI explainability service (Java/NSS, JDK 29 timeline September 2027), and the trainer data cache pending its TLS posture audit.\n- Update matrix cells as the AIPCC base availability, guardrails feasibility, and trainer posture outcomes land.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The readiness matrix covers 100% of RHOAI 3.6 payload images with all classification fields populated.\n- By September 15, 2026: zero unaccounted-for images — every image is rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base, has an in-progress switch with a linked team tracking ticket, or has a filed and acknowledged OCP exception in OCPEXCEPT documenting the component's TLS stack, why it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, and a remediation plan.\n- All component team tracking tickets are linked to the parent strategy, providing the aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0.\n- Weekly status reporting and the escalation path for teams without a plan operate through the deadline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): provides the per-image accounting that all runtime images use a PQC-enabled base image or are exception-covered.\n- HLR-2 (P0): drives the exception process so teams unable to comply by September 15 file OCP exceptions with remediation plans (per-team filing itself is out of scope; each team files its own).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78902,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1da33aad9f5aea0","agent_id":"a1b9c8d3f7c4bce05","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"21a1dc7a-1648-4393-8c17-7fcfa91322eb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:11:13.344Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
