ashboard image (largely behind a Go proxy) is the strategy's named fallback candidate for the exception route.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each python/nodejs-based runtime image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload is rebuilt with its final runtime stage based on the confirmed PQC variant, or carries a filed OCP exception.\n- For each switched image: `update-crypto-policies --show` executed inside the container reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` includes ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 (FIPS-mode clusters are exempt for RHOAI 3.6).\n- Only the final runtime stage of each Containerfile changes; no builder image is changed.\n- Build pipelines are green for all rebuilt images.\n- Base image reference changes are revertible: the previous base reference is retained so any image can be rolled back.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): delivers the PQC-enabled base image switch for the python/nodejs-based family.\n- HLR-3 (P0): enforces runtime-only enablement — final stage only, no builder image change.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":81289,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1da33aad9f5aea0","agent_id":"a1b9c8d3f7c4bce05","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"30f12127-dac8-4f8c-9a30-6b51dfa07d05","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:11:49.036Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
