{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-575eb28e-1e46-4a56-8770-208649b78018","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2df5e35a65bbbb7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-n6lpo8ou/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E009.md","content":"# Migrate trainer data cache TLS stack to an ML-KEM-capable provider (conditional)\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic migrates the trainer data cache's TLS stack to an ML-KEM (FIPS 203) capable configuration — applicable only if the TLS posture audit determines the cache uses a pure-Rust TLS stack that cannot inherit PQC from a base image swap. If the audit finds the cache is OpenSSL-backed, this epic is not needed: the PQC base image switch covers it. If the audit finds a pure-Rust stack that cannot be migrated by the September 15, 2026 deadline, the trainer team files an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with this migration as the documented remediation plan.\n\n## Scope\n\n- If required by the audit outcome: swap the data cache's TLS crypto provider to the ML-KEM-capable configuration (rustls provider and crate versions supporting X25519MLKEM768 hybrid key exchange), including dependency and feature-flag updates.\n- Extend tests to cover ML-KEM hybrid negotiation and classic ECDHE fallback for the cache's inbound and outbound connections.\n- Preserve existing TLS/mTLS configuration surfaces and operational behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- If the audit finds the cache OpenSSL-backed: this epic is closed as not-needed, with the cache accounted for by the PQC base image switch in the compliance tracking view.\n- If migrated: the data cache negotiates X25519MLKEM768 hybrid key exchange with PQC-capable peers, verified by an integration test, while non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to connect via classic ECDHE.\n- Rollback plan: the provider selection is revertible to the previous pinned configuration.\n- Build pipeline green for the rebuilt image.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): implements the remediation path if the trainer data cache cannot comply via base image swap; the exception fallback otherwise covers the component by September 15.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":82734,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1da33aad9f5aea0","agent_id":"a1b9c8d3f7c4bce05","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"7788ad8c-3287-4c1b-9c79-423a8d1f1db2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:12:08.162Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
