{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e6b10ece-21ce-46ba-ae81-800e0658a123","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a248ab07c2b7acf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-n6lpo8ou/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E011.md","content":"# TLS handshake latency regression threshold and measurement\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic closes the strategy's performance NFR, which is currently flagged as needing domain input: it defines the acceptable TLS handshake latency regression threshold (a PM + performance team lead decision the strategy requires before Sprint 2 ends), captures baseline handshake latency on current images, measures post-switch latency on PQC-rebuilt images, and publishes the pass/fail comparison. It references the Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome (PSASTRAT-7170) and the ~10% maximum TLS handshake time regression observed by Chrome as reference points.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and document the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold with the PM and performance team lead (the strategy's NFR flags this as unresolved and requires it before Sprint 2 ends).\n- Capture baseline TLS handshake latency measurements on current (non-PQC) runtime images — this proceeds independently and in parallel with the base image switch work.\n- Measure TLS handshake latency on PQC-rebuilt runtime images once switched images are available, using representative images from the switched families.\n- Compare measured regression against the agreed threshold and publish a report with methodology referencing PSASTRAT-7170 and the Chrome ~10% reference point.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold is agreed and documented with the PM and performance team lead.\n- Baseline (pre-switch) and post-switch TLS handshake latency measurements are captured for representative RHOAI runtime images, with the measurement methodology documented.\n- The measured regression is compared against the agreed threshold and a pass/fail result with supporting data is published.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (indirect): validates that the PQC base image switch meets the strategy's Performance NFR; no direct HLR — this epic implements the Performance NFR and the Performance Team Support requirement.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":84067,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1da33aad9f5aea0","agent_id":"a1b9c8d3f7c4bce05","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"9977b53b-0f27-48fb-a82b-997095caa256","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:12:29.096Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
