{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a26429e0901e975","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E011\n3\ttitle: TLS handshake latency regression threshold and measurement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: PerfScale\n6\tteam: Performance\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 0\n16\t  open_questions: -1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: Medium\n24\tai_implementability_score: 0\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# TLS handshake latency regression threshold and measurement\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic closes the strategy's performance NFR, which is currently flagged as needing domain input: it defines the acceptable TLS handshake latency regression threshold (a PM + performance team lead decision the strategy requires before Sprint 2 ends), captures baseline handshake latency on current images, measures post-switch latency on PQC-rebuilt images, and publishes the pass/fail comparison. It references the Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome (PSASTRAT-7170) and the ~10% maximum TLS handshake time regression observed by Chrome as reference points.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Define and document the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold with the PM and performance team lead (the strategy's NFR flags this as unresolved and requires it before Sprint 2 ends).\n39\t- Capture baseline TLS handshake latency measurements on current (non-PQC) runtime images — this proceeds independently and in parallel with the base image switch work.\n40\t- Measure TLS handshake latency on PQC-rebuilt runtime images once switched images are available, using representative images from the switched families.\n41\t- Compare measured regression against the agreed threshold and publish a report with methodology referencing PSASTRAT-7170 and the Chrome ~10% reference point.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold is agreed and documented with the PM and performance team lead.\n46\t- Baseline (pre-switch) and post-switch TLS handshake latency measurements are captured for representative RHOAI runtime images, with the measurement methodology documented.\n47\t- The measured regression is compared against the agreed threshold and a pass/fail result with supporting data is published.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 (indirect): validates that the PQC base image switch meets the strategy's Performance NFR; no direct HLR — this epic implements the Performance NFR and the Performance Team Support requirement.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7f46cb863dca2e5","agent_id":"a8e80f1fe8fe243da","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"7bc7be5d-744a-4ff2-a1c3-babc9f083f44","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:15:38.754Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a26429e0901e975","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
