{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4c0c9d2715a274a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E009\n3\ttitle: Migrate trainer data cache TLS stack to an ML-KEM-capable provider (conditional)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Training Kubeflow\n6\tteam: Training\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the audit finds the trainer data cache is OpenSSL-backed,\n15\t    this epic is not needed (the PQC base image switch covers it). If it uses a pure-Rust\n16\t    TLS stack that cannot be migrated by the deadline, the trainer team files an OCP\n17\t    exception via OCPEXCEPT with the migration as the remediation plan.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: -1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Low\n31\tai_implementability_score: -1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Migrate trainer data cache TLS stack to an ML-KEM-capable provider (conditional)\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic migrates the trainer data cache's TLS stack to an ML-KEM (FIPS 203) capable configuration — applicable only if the TLS posture audit determines the cache uses a pure-Rust TLS stack that cannot inherit PQC from a base image swap. If the audit finds the cache is OpenSSL-backed, this epic is not needed: the PQC base image switch covers it. If the audit finds a pure-Rust stack that cannot be migrated by the September 15, 2026 deadline, the trainer team files an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with this migration as the documented remediation plan.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- If required by the audit outcome: swap the data cache's TLS crypto provider to the ML-KEM-capable configuration (rustls provider and crate versions supporting X25519MLKEM768 hybrid key exchange), including dependency and feature-flag updates.\n44\t- Extend tests to cover ML-KEM hybrid negotiation and classic ECDHE fallback for the cache's inbound and outbound connections.\n45\t- Preserve existing TLS/mTLS configuration surfaces and operational behavior.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- If the audit finds the cache OpenSSL-backed: this epic is closed as not-needed, with the cache accounted for by the PQC base image switch in the compliance tracking view.\n50\t- If migrated: the data cache negotiates X25519MLKEM768 hybrid key exchange with PQC-capable peers, verified by an integration test, while non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to connect via classic ECDHE.\n51\t- Rollback plan: the provider selection is revertible to the previous pinned configuration.\n52\t- Build pipeline green for the rebuilt image.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-2 (P0): implements the remediation path if the trainer data cache cannot comply via base image swap; the exception fallback otherwise covers the component by September 15.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b497e7ecb7b91a47","agent_id":"a968e19c50823e180","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"19cf6f76-cb69-46eb-b4c0-0db24f191df1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:19:55.600Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4c0c9d2715a274a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
