{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bb688fbf74d7965","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n3\ttitle: Confirm AIPCC PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase commitment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AIPCC Productization\n6\tteam: AIPCC\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Confirm AIPCC PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase commitment\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's unconfirmed base image dependencies: whether PQC-enabled variants of the `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` base images will exist in time for RHOAI 3.6, and the committed date of the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase that gates adoption of `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` for the RHEL9-ELS-based image family. It tracks the AIPCC spike RHOAIENG-7195 and the rebase AIPCC-7258. The outcome determines, per image family, whether the base image switch campaigns proceed or the affected component teams file OCP exceptions by the September 15, 2026 deadline.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Engage the AIPCC team to enumerate, for each of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22`: whether a PQC variant exists today, is committed with a delivery date, or is not planned.\n34\t- For any candidate variant image that already exists, verify it activates the `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy (the same acceptance bar the strategy sets for the confirmed base images).\n35\t- Obtain the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) and assess its impact on adopting `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` for the ~34 RHEL9-ELS-based RHOAI images (notebooks, workbenches, training runtimes, mlserver).\n36\t- Produce a per-family go/no-go recommendation: switch to a PQC variant/rebased base, or fall back to component-team OCP exceptions filed via OCPEXCEPT.\n37\t- Escalate if no committed date exists by early September, per the strategy's risk mitigation.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- For each of the four python/nodejs base images, a documented availability status exists: available now (with verified `DEFAULT:PQ` policy where an image can be inspected), committed with a delivery date, or not planned.\n42\t- The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date is documented, with an explicit impact statement on RHEL9-ELS PQC base adoption for the affected image family.\n43\t- A per-family recommendation (switch vs. OCP exception fallback) is recorded and handed to the compliance tracking effort so every affected image has a decided path.\n44\t- An escalation is raised if any gating dependency has no committed date by early September 2026.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-1 (P0): determines the target PQC base image for the python-based and nodejs-based runtime images and the adoptability of the RHEL9-ELS PQC base.\n49\t- HLR-2 (P0): the per-family switch-vs-exception outcome is the decision input for teams that must file OCP exceptions by September 15.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ccd10a634b7b2f","agent_id":"a0dd64499fae42080","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"0338fd10-a64e-4f58-88ba-d7576c131d58","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:22:01.126Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bb688fbf74d7965","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
