{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93ee9e853aa3aee6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n3\ttitle: Switch ubi9-minimal-based runtime images to ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Build and Release\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Switch ubi9-minimal-based runtime images to ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic coordinates and completes the PQC base image switch for the ~68 RHOAI runtime images currently based on `ubi9/ubi-minimal:latest` — the Go operators and most platform components — by changing only the final runtime stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile to `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`. The target base image is confirmed available and reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, so this family is not gated on any external dependency and starts immediately. Per-image Dockerfile changes are executed by the owning component teams through their tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy; this epic owns the family-wide coordination, the shared build configuration updates, and accountability for family completion.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Coordinate the final-runtime-stage base switch to `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` across all ~68 ubi9-minimal-based images in the RHOAI 3.6 payload (per the RHOAI-Build-Config CSV inventory), via component team tracking tickets.\n38\t- Update shared build configuration and pipeline base image references for the family so team builds pick up the PQC base consistently.\n39\t- Enforce the runtime-only constraint: only the final stage of each Containerfile changes; no builder image changes.\n40\t- Roll up per-image switch status into the compliance tracking view; chase stragglers and trigger the exception path for any image that will not make the September 15, 2026 deadline.\n41\t- Note: Go components obtain ML-KEM via native Go crypto regardless; the base switch is done for platform consistency, per the strategy's confirmed assumption.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- All ~68 ubi9-minimal-based runtime images in the RHOAI 3.6 payload are rebuilt with the final runtime stage based on `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, or carry a filed OCP exception.\n46\t- For each switched image: `update-crypto-policies --show` executed inside the container reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` includes ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 (FIPS-mode clusters are exempt for RHOAI 3.6 — PQC deactivation under FIPS policy is expected behavior, not a compliance failure).\n47\t- Only the final runtime stage of each Containerfile changes; no builder image is changed.\n48\t- Build pipelines are green for all rebuilt images.\n49\t- Base image reference changes are revertible: the previous base reference is retained so any image can be rolled back.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-1 (P0): delivers the PQC-enabled base image switch for the ubi9-minimal family.\n54\t- HLR-3 (P0): enforces runtime-only enablement — final stage only, no builder image change.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ccd10a634b7b2f","agent_id":"a0dd64499fae42080","session_id":"2c0c1fc8-055a-4722-8bad-6dca3da0d413","uuid":"a1e08dfe-7f5d-4317-a17c-de52cea53cc1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:22:06.204Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93ee9e853aa3aee6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
